From: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 09:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: restore AN7563 TX checksum flags

The original AN7563 transmit path enables the IPv4, TCP and UDP checksum
bits together whenever an skb requests partial checksum offload.  The
unified path instead parses the packet and enables only the matching
protocol bits.

Restore the original descriptor flags on AN7563, including for TSO skbs,
while retaining the protocol-specific handling on the other SoCs.

Signed-off-by: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -7419,6 +7419,13 @@ static netdev_tx_t __airoha_dev_xmit
 		       FIELD_PREP(QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_SP_TAG_MASK, tag);
 	}
-	if (!xpon_oam)
-		msg0 |= airoha_qdma_tx_csum_flags(skb);
+	if (!xpon_oam) {
+		if (airoha_is(qdma->eth, airoha_an7563) &&
+		    skb->ip_summed == CHECKSUM_PARTIAL)
+			msg0 |= QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_TCO_MASK |
+				QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_UCO_MASK |
+				QDMA_ETH_TXMSG_ICO_MASK;
+		else
+			msg0 |= airoha_qdma_tx_csum_flags(skb);
+	}
 
 	/* TSO: fill MSS info in tcp checksum field */
-- 
